<title>USA: Redwood Financial drops repurchase effort.</title>
<headline>Redwood Financial drops repurchase effort.</headline>
<dateline>REDWOOD FALLS, Minn. 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Redwood Financial Inc said Tuesday it has withdrawn its request for regulatory approval of a second stock repurchase program.</p>
<p>The company had been advised by federal regulators that the request, covering an additional 10 percent of the company's common shares, was unlikely to be approved, a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>Redwood Financial, the parent of Redwoood Falls Federal Savings and Loan Association, completed a separate 10 percent stock buyback program, approved in September, last week.</p>
<p>The company's shares closed down 3/8 at 11-1/2.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
